<div class="page">
  <div class="container" style="max-width:44rem;">
    <div class="section-head">
      <p class="overline">Legal</p>
      <h1 class="page-title">Privacy Policy</h1>
      <p class="section-sub">Last updated <%= getYear() %></p>
    </div>

    <div class="stack" style="gap:var(--sp-6);">
      <section>
        <h2 class="card-title">What we collect</h2>
        <ul class="muted" style="margin-top:var(--sp-2);display:grid;gap:var(--sp-2);padding-left:1.1rem;">
          <li><strong>Account:</strong> your name (optional), email address and a hashed password. We never see or store your password in plain text.</li>
          <li><strong>Reading activity:</strong> the last chapter you opened in each book, so the app can offer to resume. Stored against your account.</li>
          <li><strong>Payments:</strong> order id, amount and status, so we can confirm your subscription and administer refunds.</li>
          <li><strong>Preferences:</strong> your light/dark theme choice, selected text-to-speech voice and playback speed. These live only in your browser's local storage and are never sent to us.</li>
        </ul>
      </section>

      <section>
        <h2 class="card-title">What we do not collect</h2>
        <p class="muted" style="margin-top:var(--sp-2);">
          We do not use advertising trackers, we do not sell your data, and we do not build profiles
          of your reading habits. We do not see the content of any search you run.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section>
        <h2 class="card-title">Cookies</h2>
        <p class="muted" style="margin-top:var(--sp-2);">
          One cookie is set: a signed session cookie that keeps you signed in and protects against
          cross-site request forgery. It contains an opaque session identifier only.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section>
        <h2 class="card-title">Payments</h2>
        <p class="muted" style="margin-top:var(--sp-2);">
          Card and UPI details are entered on Razorpay's own checkout. We receive only a confirmation
          that a payment succeeded — never your card number.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section>
        <h2 class="card-title">Your rights</h2>
        <p class="muted" style="margin-top:var(--sp-2);">
          You can request a copy of your data or ask for your account to be deleted at any time by
          emailing <a href="mailto:support@upscbooks.shop">support@upscbooks.shop</a>. Deleting your
          account removes your profile, reading progress and subscription records.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section>
        <h2 class="card-title">Contact</h2>
        <p class="muted" style="margin-top:var(--sp-2);">
          Privacy questions: <a href="mailto:support@upscbooks.shop">support@upscbooks.shop</a>.
        </p>
      </section>
    </div>
  </div>
</div>